{"title":"neon glow comfort, sagitarrius ii","link":"https://keningzhu.com/journal/neon-glow-comfort-sagitarrius-ii","date":1766000400000,"content":"<figure>\n          \n        \n        \n\n        \n          \n            \n          \n            \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                <img src=\"https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/82562e43-73ed-4856-81a4-6f72dbe55a2f/sag+ii.png?format=1000w\" width=\"3840\" height=\"2160\" srcset=\"https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/82562e43-73ed-4856-81a4-6f72dbe55a2f/sag+ii.png?format=100w 100w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/82562e43-73ed-4856-81a4-6f72dbe55a2f/sag+ii.png?format=300w 300w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/82562e43-73ed-4856-81a4-6f72dbe55a2f/sag+ii.png?format=500w 500w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/82562e43-73ed-4856-81a4-6f72dbe55a2f/sag+ii.png?format=750w 750w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/82562e43-73ed-4856-81a4-6f72dbe55a2f/sag+ii.png?format=1000w 1000w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/82562e43-73ed-4856-81a4-6f72dbe55a2f/sag+ii.png?format=1500w 1500w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/82562e43-73ed-4856-81a4-6f72dbe55a2f/sag+ii.png?format=2500w 2500w\" loading=\"lazy\" />\n\n            \n          \n        \n          \n        \n\n        \n      \n        </figure>\n      \n\n    \n  \n\n\n  \n\n\n \n\n\n  <p><em>this series is created for my collaboration with </em><a href=\"https://www.ceremony-studio.co.uk/\" target=\"_blank\"><em>LJ of Ceremony</em></a><em> for their communal writing practice, </em><a href=\"https://www.ceremony-studio.co.uk/atmospheres\" target=\"_blank\"><em>Atmospheres</em></a><em>, based of the 36 decans of the astrological year. </em></p>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n  \n\n\n\n<hr />\n\n\n  <p><strong>Sagitarrius II</strong> — Dec 1-11<br /><strong>Key themes from LJ</strong> — luminosity, artificial light, spectacle<br /><strong>Before this: </strong><a href=\"https://keningonline.squarespace.com/journal/questing-for-the-grail-sagitarrius-i\">questing for the grail, sagitarrius i</a><a href=\"https://keningzhu.com/journal/dosing-the-poison-cure-scorpio-ii\"><br /></a><br />*</p><p>for this decan, I wanted to capture the energy of neon lights, luminescent mushrooms, and the energy of being always “on” — activated, lit, unable to totally dissolve into the black cosmos. there is comfort in this uncanny light. it is almost a sort of reassurance that, even in darkness, if all else fails, there <em>will</em> be an energy source, however artificial. neon lights can feel very cheap and consumerist, or strangely romantic; even nostalgic. </p>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n  \n\n\n\n<hr />\n\n\n  <h1>process</h1>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n  \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n\n    \n  \n    \n\n      \n\n      \n        <figure>\n          \n        \n        \n\n        \n          \n            \n          \n            \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                <img src=\"https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/3f313754-ebc7-4ed5-b81e-fc750275e44c/sagii-ezgif.com-optimize.gif?format=1000w\" width=\"800\" height=\"450\" srcset=\"https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/3f313754-ebc7-4ed5-b81e-fc750275e44c/sagii-ezgif.com-optimize.gif?format=100w 100w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/3f313754-ebc7-4ed5-b81e-fc750275e44c/s